2026-11-05T19:39:00.4208020Z CLANG_CONFIG_FILE_SYSTEM_DIR: /opt/homebrew/etc/clang
2026-11-05T19:39:00.4318640Z CLANG_CONFIG_FILE_USER_DIR:   ~/.config/clang
2026-11-05T19:39:00.4439010Z 
2026-11-05T19:39:00.4541310Z LLD and LLDB are now provided in separate formulae:
2026-11-05T19:39:00.4647130Z   brew install lld
2026-11-05T19:39:00.4754940Z   brew install lldb
2026-11-05T19:39:00.4794500Z 
2026-11-05T19:39:00.4815000Z Z3 solver support will be removed in LLVM 24 as it is unsupported upstream,
2026-11-05T19:39:00.4858070Z see https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/pull/205370
2026-11-05T19:39:00.4864490Z 
2026-11-05T19:39:00.4868200Z Using `clang`, `clang++`, etc., requires a CLT installation at `/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools`.
2026-11-05T19:39:00.4877440Z If you don't want to install the CLT, you can write appropriate configuration files pointing to your
2026-11-05T19:39:00.4980410Z SDK at ~/.config/clang.
2026-11-05T19:39:00.5022060Z 
2026-11-05T19:39:00.5043570Z To use the bundled libunwind please use the following LDFLAGS:
2026-11-05T19:39:00.5044330Z   LDFLAGS="-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/unwind -lunwind"
2026-11-05T19:39:00.5044590Z 
2026-11-05T19:39:00.5044990Z To use the bundled libc++ please use the following LDFLAGS:
2026-11-05T19:39:00.5048020Z   LDFLAGS="-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/c++ -L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/unwind -lunwind"
2026-11-05T19:39:00.5051780Z Features newer than system libc++ will require the following define to enable
2026-11-05T19:39:00.5053470Z (support for this may be removed in a future major LLVM release):
2026-11-05T19:39:00.5056290Z   CPPFLAGS="-D_LIBCPP_DISABLE_AVAILABILITY"
2026-11-05T19:39:00.5057190Z 
2026-11-05T19:39:00.5058150Z NOTE: You probably want to use the libunwind and libc++ provided by macOS unless you know what you're doing.
2026-11-05T19:39:00.5060500Z 
2026-11-05T19:39:00.5061150Z llvm is keg-only, which means it was not symlinked into /opt/homebrew,
2026-11-05T19:39:00.5063110Z because macOS already provides this software and installing another version in
2026-11-05T19:39:00.5064430Z parallel can cause all kinds of trouble.
2026-11-05T19:39:00.5065180Z 
2026-11-05T19:39:00.5065770Z If you need to have llvm first in your PATH, run:
2026-11-05T19:39:00.5068440Z   printf '%s\n' export\ PATH\=/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/bin:\$PATH >> /Users/runner/.bash_profile
2026-11-05T19:39:00.5070210Z 
2026-11-05T19:39:00.5070650Z For compilers to find llvm you may need to set:
2026-11-05T19:39:00.5075970Z   export LDFLAGS=-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib
2026-11-05T19:39:00.5077500Z   export CPPFLAGS=-I/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/include
2026-11-05T19:39:00.5077930Z 
2026-11-05T19:39:00.5078590Z For cmake to find llvm you may need to set:
2026-11-05T19:39:00.5081060Z   export CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm
